Fyrdelf 11 (fyrdelf:11) 120x60
stairs Up at (88, 50) -> fyrdelf:10
stairs Down at (24, 17) -> fyrdelf:12
special room teeming at (108, 49)-(113, 58)
place a hooded figure at (80, 33): Its empty hands are held as if about a hilt that is not there. Letters are cut deep into the plinth, in the old tongue: LĪF ǢR DĒAÞE. Below, in a later hand: 'Life before death. So the hunters swore, to the one who waited for them on the road; and the road gave them each a blade.'
